[size=5][b]FaceLab[/b][/size]
[i]RaceMenu-style face morphs, live in the game world - on you or on any NPC. A tool for players, and a face API for mod authors.[/i]

[size=4][b]What is it?[/b][/size]
RaceMenu has expression sliders (Smile, Sad, Angry, BigAah ...) that go up to 3.0, far beyond what the game's face animation ever uses. FaceLab plays those same morphs [b]live in the world[/b], held while a scene runs, faded in and out, and layered between mods. You can try expressions on yourself or on an NPC, and other mods can ask for a named face ("pleased", "shocked", "tongue out") without writing any face code.

[b]On its own FaceLab changes nothing in your game.[/b] It is a lab, and the thing other mods plug into.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Skyrim SE 1.5.97, or AE 1.6.x / 1.7.x (one DLL, Address Library). [b]Only AE 1.6.1170 has been tested by me[/b]; the other versions are supported through the Address Library but untested
[*]SKSE and the matching Address Library
[*]SKSE Menu Framework (the FaceLab menu lives in it)
[*][b]A head with morph files.[/b] FaceLab ships none, it reads the ones you already have:
[/list]
[table]
[tr][td][b]Head[/b][/td][td][b]Needs[/b][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]High Poly Head (male / female)[/td][td]High Poly Head[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Vanilla head (male / female)[/td][td]Expressive Facial Animation[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]CoTR [b]original low poly[/b] head (male / female)[/td][td]CoTR's expression files. The CoTR High Poly head is [b]not[/b] supported[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]UBE (female)[/td][td]UBE 2.0[/td][/tr]
[/table]
Heads that have extra morphs (CoTR's Smile001..., UBE's Ahegao, Kiss, Yawning...) show them as extra sliders automatically. A head FaceLab does not know is reported as "not supported" in the log and left alone.

[size=4][b]Using it (players)[/b][/size]
Open the SKSE Menu Framework menu and choose [b]FaceLab[/b]. Six pages (Face, Assists, Presets, Scenes, Controls, Debug):
[b]Face[/b]
[list]
[*]Pick the target: the player, or the NPC you last looked at (close the menu, look at them, reopen it).
[*]Move the sliders (0-300, which is the RaceMenu weight x 100; 300 = 3.0). Press [i]Apply all sliders[/i], or tick "apply as soon as I move it". [i]Reset the target's face[/i] takes it off.
[*]A face you apply here outranks every other mod's face and lets go by itself after the "holds for" time (0 = until Reset).
[*]Start with [i]Just BigAah 3.0[/i] to check that it works on your target.
[/list]
[b]Assists[/b] - helpers that sit on top of the face: mouth assist, the tongue's "how far out", oral assist, and eye assists (limits and lid follow for add-on eyes, plus a per-direction correction for UBE eyes).
[b]Presets[/b] - the named faces other mods use. Load one into the sliders to see it, change it, and save it back or as a new name. They are plain text files in [font=Courier New]Data/SKSE/Plugins/FaceLab/Presets[/font].
[b]Scenes[/b] - built-in rules that put a face on the people in an OStim or SexLab scene.
[b]Controls[/b] - one hotkey (keyboard or gamepad, with modifier) that applies the sliders and, on the next press, resets. Default gamepad: X while holding D-pad Down. An optional second hotkey shows and hides the tongue.
[b]Debug[/b] - probe, poke and hide-a-shape tests for finding a problem. Off for normal use.

A face is [b]never saved[/b]: a new game or a load drops every face, so nothing can get stuck in your save.

[size=4][b]Special channels[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]TongueOut[/b] - the face asks a [b]tongue mod[/b] for the tongue. FaceLab draws no tongue itself: without a tongue mod this slider does nothing
[*][b]OralMode[/b] - 50 or more marks an oral scene: the mouth belongs to OStim, FaceLab's mouth gives way
[*][b]MouthAssist[/b] - an opening that fades out as the natural mouth opens
[*][b]EyesCross[/b] - The Fourth Wall lets go of the eyes while this is on
[/list]

[size=4][b]For mod authors[/b][/size]
Ship a text file of named faces, then ask for one by name from Papyrus or from an SKSE plugin:
[code]
; Data/SKSE/Plugins/FaceLab/Presets/MyMod.toml
[[preset]]
name = "MyMod.Kissing.Pleased"
weights = { MoodHappy = 120, BigAah = 40 }

; Papyrus
FaceLab.ApplyFace(akActor, "MyMod", "MyMod.Kissing.Pleased", 0.5, 10)
FaceLab.ClearFace(akActor, "MyMod", 0.5)
[/code]
Your face is a layer owned by your mod: the highest priority wins, clearing removes only yours, and a missing "Displeased" or "Pleased" falls back to "Neutral". There is a C++ header too (no link library), lip-sync yield, mouth/tongue/eye read-backs and a gaze layer. The API files are [b]MIT[/b]: using them does not put your mod under the GPL, and if FaceLab is missing your calls simply do nothing.
Full guide: [i]MODDER_GUIDE.md[/i] in the downloads and on GitHub.

[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]
Open [font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/FaceLab.log[/font]. The line [i]"Morph: &lt;name&gt; uses head family '...'"[/i] means it works on that actor. [i]"is not supported: none of the head families fits"[/i] means the head, or its morph mod, is not one of the supported ones. Scattered lines or a deformed head [b]in RaceMenu itself[/b] mean two morph mods overwrite each other (different vertex counts) - a load order problem, not FaceLab. If you report something, tick [i]Debug tools[/i] on the Face page first and attach the log.

[size=4][b]Compatible with[/b][/size]
OStim scene mods (scene faces), tongue mods (TongueOut), The Fourth Wall (EyesCross, gaze), SMP physics and RaceMenu. Nothing is written to your save.

[size=4][b]Licence and source[/b][/size]
FaceLab is free software, [b]GPL-3.0-or-later[/b]. Source: [url=https://github.com/bolescothegoat/FaceLab]github.com/bolescothegoat/FaceLab[/url]. The two API files (C++ header and Papyrus script) are MIT.
Built on CommonLibSSE-NG (alandtse), SKSE Menu Framework, spdlog, fmt, toml++ and DirectXTK (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES). The morph mods above belong to their authors and are required, not included.

[size=4][b]Changelog[/b][/size]
[b]0.2.2[/b] - Built-in scene rules for OStim and SexLab (new Scenes page; SexLab support is untested by the author), with an optional Starter Scenes download. Add-on eyes (Advanced Eyes Addon) work, with new Eye assist sliders. UBE eye sliders (% change, 0 = calibrated). New Assists page; the tongue has an on/off button, a hotkey and a "how far out" slider. "Do it" is now "Apply", Debug tools have their own page. Update FaceLab and your tongue mod together.
[b]0.2.1[/b] - Faster: a face update is about five times cheaper (a memory check that ran on every update is now done once), so FaceLab costs a fraction of a millisecond per frame even with several characters. Faces look exactly as before.
[b]0.2.0[/b] - First public release.
